- Required SUB-bit transitions while traversing nested DUP cells.
- Whether `heap_take/heap_set` ordering constraints exist for determinism/races (single-threaded AOT path still uses shared heap primitives).
- Whether there are counterexamples where DP composition changes observable behavior (e.g., interaction counts allowed to differ, but term/linearity must remain identical).
- If composition is valid only for a subset, which tag/configuration boundaries should force fallback immediately.
